| !Run for !ReelEGL (Reel drawing through riscos-mesa's EGL)
| Puts ReelEGL on the icon bar. Drop a video on it (or a file of web
| addresses, such as yt-dlp's output), or double-click a video in the
| Filer while ReelEGL is loaded. %*0 = a file to play at once.
Set ReelEGL$Dir <Obey$Dir>
| *ReelEGL <a video, or a web address> plays it: for a command line, or another
| program handing it a stream (as for mplayer and ffplay)
SetMacro Alias$ReelEGL /<ReelEGL$Dir> %%*0
IconSprites <ReelEGL$Dir>.!Sprites

RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error ReelEGL needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error ReelEGL needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
| Threads: the thread timer of UnixLib 5.0.1 and later (which ReelEGL is built with)
| runs from the PThreadTicker module when it's loaded: a copy merged into
| !System first, else the one in here. Without it UnixLib uses a copy in
| the RMA, which also works.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere <ReelEGL$Dir>.PThrTicker Then RMLoad <ReelEGL$Dir>.PThrTicker
| Web addresses (https): RISC OS's AcornSSL module (RISC OS 5.28 or
| later); quiet if it's missing (then http:// only)
RMEnsure AcornSSL 0 IfThere System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL Then RMLoad System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL
| Hardware acceleration: the VideoOverlay module (in !System on RISC OS 5);
| quiet if it's missing (then the picture is drawn as before)
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay
| Sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager (ssb.zip, from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html) and SharedSound
| (part of RISC OS). Merged into !System they still have to be loaded:
| these do it (and are quiet if they're missing).
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| The program is about 37MB (it includes riscos-mesa's EGL and OpenGL);
| its memory for pictures and sound is in a dynamic area ("ReelEGL Heap").
WimpSlot -min 49152K -max 49152K
| Log (<Wimp$ScrapDir>.ReelEGLLog; Log on the icon bar menu opens it): off in
| release builds, as it costs a little time while playing. For one, put a |
| in front of the next line. (Test builds come with it commented out. A
| *Set ReelEGL$Log <file> of your own is left alone.)
If "<ReelEGL$Log>"="" Then Set ReelEGL$Log off
Run <ReelEGL$Dir>.!RunImage %*0
